<div class="card">
  <div class="card-header">
    <h2>How GatherPack Got Started</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <p>
      GatherPack started as a quick fix for a <a href="https://boilerinvasion.org" target="_blank">FIRST Robotics team</a> that couldn't keep its information straight. Attendance records, fundraising progress, and competition logistics were scattered across spreadsheets, sticky notes, and the heads of whoever happened to be available to ask.
      <a href="https://brad-thompson.com" target="_blank">One volunteer web developer</a> built a small internal tool to pull it together, and watched it grow over the next decade into the operational backbone of <a href="https://westside-robotics.info" target="_blank">an organization</a> that has since quadrupled in size.
    </p>
    <p>
      When that original tool started showing its age, the same developer and a few students rebuilt it from scratch, this time with other organizations in mind. The goal was something flexible and capable enough to handle not just what their team needed, but what any group like theirs might need.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-header">
    <h2>Built by the Community, for the Community</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <p>
      GatherPack's features are shaped by organizations that actually use it every day.
      Most group management tools are built around simple membership lists and basic announcements. GatherPack goes further, handling the coordination work that active organizations actually deal with: tracking who showed up, managing shared finances, running events, and giving more than just the top admins the ability to contribute.
      It's designed to grow with your organization rather than locking you into one particular way of doing things.
    </p>
    <p>
      GatherPack is free, open source software. If your organization has some technical chops, you can self-host and customize it at no cost.
      If you'd rather have someone else handle those technical bits, we've partnered with <a href="https://sledgehammerinfosystems.com" target="_blank">Sledgehammer Infosystems</a> to offer a variety of managed hosting and service options.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

